<!-- HERO -->
<section class="hero" id="individuals">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="section-eyebrow with-rule">For you &amp; your family</span>
        <h1 class="hero-title">Protection that picks up <span class="em">before you do.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">זוג אוזניים נוסף בכל שיחה. זוג עיניים נוסף בכל הודעה. בנוי לאנשים שהכי מותקפים — ובני המשפחה שדואגים להם.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <a href="protection-plans.html" class="btn btn-accent">קבלו הגנה
            <svg width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </a>
          <a href="#feel" class="btn btn-ink">See how it feels</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="phone-card" aria-label="Live call alert example">
        <div style="display:inline-block;margin-bottom:14px;padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--accent);border-radius:3px;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:700;font-size:.58rem;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent);background:rgba(190,58,75,.06)">Illustrative example</div>
        <div class="phone-head">
          <span class="live"><span class="dot"></span>Incoming call</span>
          <span class="time">00:09</span>
        </div>
        <p class="phone-caller">Caller ID claims</p>
        <p class="phone-name">"Mum"</p>
        <p class="phone-verdict">Voice does <strong>not match Mum's</strong> previous calls. Likely AI clone.</p>
        <dl class="phone-bits">
          <dt>Voice</dt><dd><strong>94% synthetic</strong></dd>
          <dt>Number</dt><dd>Unknown · not in contacts</dd>
          <dt>Pattern</dt><dd>Urgency + money request</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="phone-actions">
          <button class="phone-btn primary" type="button">End call</button>
          <button class="phone-btn" type="button">Call Mum back</button>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- WHO IS THIS FOR -->
<section class="who">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="who-grid">
      <div class="who-meta">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">למי זה מתאים</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">אם אי פעם הרגשתם את הפניקה — זה בשבילכם.</h2>
        <p class="who-meta-note">ליחידים · למשפחות · למטפלים</p>
      </div>
      <div class="who-body">
        <p class="lead">The most expensive moment in a scam isn't the wire — it's the thirty seconds before, when a clear-headed person is being walked into a decision they would never normally make.</p>
        <p>You are not the weak link. You're being attacked by a script that has worked on thousands of people who do not consider themselves gullible — because it isn't about gullibility, it's about <em>timing, pressure and fear</em>.</p>
        <p>ASPS sits next to you in that moment. Not blocking, not deciding — just showing you what's actually on the other end of the line, and giving you the seconds back to choose.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- TWO DOORS — individuals / families -->
<section class="doors" id="families">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="doors-head">
      <span class="section-eyebrow with-rule">שני דרכים לכניסה</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">לעצמכם, או למישהו שאתם אוהבים.</h2>
      <p>אותה הגנה, מוגדרת בשתי דרכים שונות לפי מי שאתם דואגים לו היום.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doors-grid">
      <article class="door">
        <p class="door-tag">לעצמכם</p>
        <h3>הגנו <span class="em">על הקו שלכם.</span></h3>
        <p class="door-lede">Calls, messages, emails and the websites you click. One layer across everything that reaches you, working quietly until something is wrong.</p>
        <ul class="door-list">
          <li>Real-time AI voice detection on every call</li>
          <li>SMS, WhatsApp &amp; email screening</li>
          <li><strong>Explainable alerts</strong> — never a black box</li>
          <li>One-tap safe actions: end call, freeze transaction</li>
          <li>Private by default — your data, your device first</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="door-foot">
          <span>יחיד · מ‑€4.90 לחודש</span>
          <a href="#pricing">ראו תוכניות</a>
          <a href="contact.html?subject=individual" class="door-talk">דברו איתנו →</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="door">
        <p class="door-tag">למשפחה שלכם</p>
        <h3>הרחיבו את זה <span class="em">לאנשים שאתם דואגים להם.</span></h3>
        <p class="door-lede">Parents, grandparents, kids. Same protection, but with you in the loop — opt-in, always visible, never silent surveillance.</p>
        <ul class="door-list">
          <li>Up to 6 family members on one plan</li>
          <li>You're alerted when <strong>their</strong> phone is alerted</li>
          <li>Safe-word verification you can agree on together</li>
          <li>Easy-mode UI for non-technical users</li>
          <li>Consent-first — your relative installs and approves</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="door-foot">
          <span>משפחה · מ‑€9.90 לחודש</span>
          <a href="#pricing">ראו תוכניות</a>
          <a href="contact.html?subject=family" class="door-talk">דברו איתנו →</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- PROTECTS — channels -->
<section class="protects">
  <div class="protects-inner">
    <div class="protects-head">
      <div>
        <span class="section-eyebrow">מה זה מגן</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">בכל מקום שנוכל יכול להגיע אליכם.</h2>
      </div>
      <span class="protects-head-meta">Four surfaces · One quiet layer</span>
    </div>
    <div class="protects-grid">
      <div class="protect"><p class="protect-tag">01 / Calls</p><h3 class="protect-title">Phone calls</h3><p class="protect-body">Real-time voice analysis flags AI-cloned voices, impersonators and pressure scripts — while the call is happening.</p></div>
      <div class="protect"><p class="protect-tag">02 / Messages</p><h3 class="protect-title">Text &amp; chat</h3><p class="protect-body">SMS, WhatsApp and messaging apps scanned for phishing links, urgency patterns and impersonated senders.</p></div>
      <div class="protect"><p class="protect-tag">03 / Mail</p><h3 class="protect-title">Email</h3><p class="protect-body">Spoofed senders, dangerous attachments and social-engineering threads — flagged before you reply.</p></div>
      <div class="protect"><p class="protect-tag">04 / Web</p><h3 class="protect-title">Browser</h3><p class="protect-body">Fake bank pages, shopping scams and malicious downloads caught at the moment of click.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- HOW IT FEELS -->
<section class="feel" id="feel">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="feel-head">
      <span class="section-eyebrow with-rule">איך זה מרגיש</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">שלושה רגעים, כתף שקטה אחת.</h2>
      <p>Three real-world situations, and what ASPS does in each — written the way they actually happen, not the way they look in brochures.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="feel-grid">
      <div class="feel-row">
        <span class="feel-num"></span>
        <span class="feel-when">Tuesday · 14:42</span>
        <div>
          <h3>"This is the bank's <span class="em">fraud team.</span>"</h3>
          <p>The voice is calm, official, and knows your last four digits. They need you to move money to "a safe account" — right now.</p>
          <p>ASPS reads the voice (flagged as synthetic), checks the number (not your bank's), and the script (matches known impersonation patterns). The verdict lands on screen before they finish the sentence.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="feel-row">
        <span class="feel-num"></span>
        <span class="feel-when">Saturday · 21:08</span>
        <div>
          <h3>A text from your <span class="em">"son."</span></h3>
          <p>New number. "Hi Dad, my phone broke, can you send €600 to this account by tomorrow morning, please don't tell Mum."</p>
          <p>ASPS recognises the cadence — a templated message pattern that's been circulating widely this month. It surfaces the warning, the alternate verification path, and a one-tap call to your actual son's known number.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="feel-row">
        <span class="feel-num"></span>
        <span class="feel-when">Sunday · 11:14</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Mum is on the phone — <span class="em">except she isn't.</span></h3>
          <p>Her voice. Her cadence. Crying. "I've had an accident, please don't tell Dad, I just need money for the lawyer."</p>
          <p>You get a quiet alert on your phone too — the family layer fired. Voice profile doesn't match her usual baseline. You call her real number while still listening. She picks up. She's fine.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

