<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="faq-head">
      <span class="section-eyebrow with-rule">שאלות שאנשים שואלים</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">תשובות כנות לדברים שחשובים.</h2>
    </div>

    <ul class="faq-list">
      <li><details><summary>Does ASPS listen to all my phone calls?</summary><p>It analyses audio on your device while a call is active — looking for synthetic-voice signatures, impersonation patterns and known scam scripts. The audio itself is not stored or sent to our servers. Verdicts and patterns are; the content of your conversation isn't.</p></details></li>
      <li><details><summary>Will it block my real bank when they call?</summary><p>No. ASPS doesn't block calls — it shows you what it sees and lets you decide. When a number genuinely belongs to your bank, that's part of the signal, not against it. You always have the final say.</p></details></li>
      <li><details><summary>Can I set this up for a parent who isn't tech-savvy?</summary><p>Yes — the Family plan is built for exactly that. You install once, your relative confirms on their device (consent is required), and after that the interface is reduced to the simplest possible alert. They never have to interpret a dashboard.</p></details></li>
      <li><details><summary>What happens to the data ASPS sees?</summary><p>Pattern data and verdicts are kept; raw audio and message bodies aren't. Anything that does leave your device is encrypted, region-pinned, and never sold. The full data policy is on the privacy page.</p></details></li>
      <li><details><summary>Does it work on iPhone, Android, or both?</summary><p>Both. Some channels (calls especially) integrate more deeply on Android due to platform limits on iOS — the differences are listed transparently when you set up each device.</p></details></li>
      <li><details><summary>Can I cancel any time?</summary><p>Yes — monthly billing, cancel from the app, no exit fees, no "win-back" calls.</p></details></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- PULL QUOTE -->
<section class="pullquote-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="pullquote">
      <p class="pullquote-text">The point isn't catching scams. The point is <strong>the next thirty seconds</strong> — what you do, before money or trust changes hands.</p>
      <span class="pullquote-cite">— ASPS Platform Principles</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

